# SLAYER TERMINAL — data providers
#
# Copy to `.env` and fill in. `.env` is gitignored; this file is not, so it
# must never hold a real key.
#
# TWO WAYS TO CONFIGURE, and they are not equivalent.
#
# 1. PROXIED (ship this one). VITE_DATA_PROXY points at a server you control
#    that holds the real keys and forwards to the vendors. The browser never
#    sees a secret. When it is set it wins over everything below.
#
#    The proxy is expected to expose:
#       <proxy>/polygon/<path>          → https://api.massive.com/<path>
#       <proxy>/unusualwhales/<path>    → https://api.unusualwhales.com/<path>
#       <proxy>/<provider>/socket       → the vendor's websocket
#
# VITE_DATA_PROXY=https://data.your-host.example
#
# 2. DIRECT (development only). Vite INLINES any VITE_-prefixed variable into
#    the shipped bundle, so a key set this way is readable by anyone who opens
#    the network tab. Use it with a key you are willing to expose and can
#    rotate, never with one you are not.

# Polygon / Massive — Stocks Advanced, Options Advanced, Indices Advanced,
# Currencies Starter, NYSE Order Imbalances
# VITE_POLYGON_KEY=

# Unusual Whales — API Advanced
# VITE_UW_KEY=
